WEBVTT

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.120
Good grief.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:21.130
Ta-dah!

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.430
Shiny and sparkly!

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.810
Oh, yeah!

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.780
Ooh!

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.280
I found a fun little bug!

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:45.570
It's that late already?

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:52.830
Good morning, ladies.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.290
This is today's update.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.250
Thanks to the maintenance group's hard work for the past week,

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.340
we now have a functioning bath.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.880
It will be ready to use at noon today.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:05.300
Yay!

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.300
A bath! A bath!

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.310
They built it outside,
overlooking the Adriatic Sea.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.600
Oh? An open-air bath, huh?

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.940
Yeah. Sanya's going to be so excited.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:23.150
You're all off duty today. Please tell everyone about the bath.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:24.160
Yes, ma'am!

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.030
Isn't that great, Yoshika-chan?

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.240
Yeah. Let's take a bath together.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.080
You should join us, too, Perrine-san.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:30.370
Hmm?

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:34.620
W-Well, it is nice to take a relaxing bath, after working up a sweat.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.790
A bath! A bath!

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.420
I'm gonna be the first one-

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.300
Weren't you paying attention?

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.710
The bath won't be ready until noon.

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.640
What? I can't use it yet?

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.970
We still have time before
we can take our baths...

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:53.390
Which means there is something we
can do to make them more enjoyable.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:55.900
What is it, Sakamoto-san?

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.980
Work up a sweat with some drills!

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:01.320
Everyone, run laps around the base!

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:04.650
But we can do drills anyti-

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.240
I don't want to hear
another word. Run!

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.450
Yes, ma'am...

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:14.540
Sheesh... Why is everyone so excited over taking a bath?

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:19.130
If it gives them some new energy, I don't see any harm in it.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.800
You look tired, yourself.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:27.890
I feel like I've been battling my
superiors more than the Neuroi lately.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:31.390
That's right. Recently, you haven't been able to join us in battle, huh?

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:33.350
You haven't shot down
many Neuroi lately, either.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:37.230
I've been stuck at 199 for a while now.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.150
I guess when I hit two hundred, I'll be given a medal or something.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:43.360
Frankly, I'd rather they just lowered the amount of paperwork I have.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:46.610
You'll melt your exhaustion
away if you take a warm bath.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.910
Why not join me, Minna?

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:53.580
Well, I still have some
paperwork I need to file...

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.620
I'll think about it.
Thanks for the offer.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.380
I see. Don't work too hard.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.050
A bug? What's it look like?

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:09.760
Okay, so... It's like
this big... And it's so shiny!

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.680
I'll show it to you later!

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:14.810
Wow... I can't wait!

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:45.420
A power outage?

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.400
I don't care who you are.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:09.650
I will not tolerate someone crossing the Siegfried line!

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.780
Wake up, Hartmann! Morning's over!

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.700
Just give me forty more minutes...

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.500
Again with the "forty minutes"? What does that even mean?!

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.710
Th-There's no place to get my footing...

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:30.380
What?

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.590
Damn!

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:34.430
Hartmann, wake up!

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.390
Wake up and do something!

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.310
Just give me fifty more minutes...

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:44.480
Wake up!

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:47.730
Huh?

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.490
My Siegfried line!

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:00.330
Hey! Hartmann! Wake up!

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.840
All right. It's ready.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:08.880
You can use the bath now.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.880
A bath! A bath! A bath! A bath!

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:14.970
What's the matter, Perrine?

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.010
Huh?

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.600
You aren't going in?

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:20.060
U-Um, are you also going, Major?

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:24.020
Oh, right. I washed myself
in a tub after morning drills,

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.350
so I'm good for today.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:26.310
Huh?

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:28.690
I-I see...

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:40.330
Wow!

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:43.210
First one in!

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.000
Second one in!

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.380
This is the best!

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.380
It feels so nice...

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.470
Hop in already, Lynne-chan!

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:54.880
R-Right...

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.890
Why are you being so modest?

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:08.980
What do you think
you're doing, Eila-san?!

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:12.570
Oh, Lynne, have you gone up a size?

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:15.530
Lemme feel 'em.

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.360
Squishy, squishy, squishy.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:20.450
Knock it off, Eila-san!

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.330
Lemme feel 'em, Yoshika.

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:26.420
I'm disappointed.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:27.540
Disappointed?

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:29.460
What do you mean, disappointed?!

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:31.550
Squishy, squishy, squishy.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:34.130
You animals!

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:44.560
Ah... That was so relaxing.

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:46.940
I'm gonna take another
one with Shirley later!

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:50.360
I wonder if Sanya's
gonna wake up soon.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:54.360
My goodness! Who taught you guys your bath time manners?

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.700
Stripes!

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.460
Huh?

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:19.760
No!

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.390
Wh-What's wrong?

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:26.560
Th-There's something in my pants...

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:30.850
What is that? A bug?

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:31.980
Bug?!

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:37.150
N-N-No!

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:39.450
It flew away!

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:40.110
What happened?

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.830
H-How horrifying!

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:46.040
Huh? Why's everyone getting all freaked out over a little bug-

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:49.670
Eila-san?

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:53.090
There's something in my pants...

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:54.340
You mean...

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.630
It's gotta be the bug!

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:56.300
Bug?

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:57.170
Let us see!

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.170
Bug!

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.550
D-D-Don't come near me.

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:06.390
J-Just horrifying.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.310
Oh, I recognize that bug.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:09.350
Really, now...

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:12.020
Bugs going into people's pants? Seriously?

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:16.400
If you guys didn't live such filthy
lives, maybe that wouldn't happen.

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.410
It went over to Perrine-san!

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.120
That's my bug!

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:29.450
Y-You're mistaken.
A bug didn't go inside my-

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:33.830
N-Not in there!

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:34.920
Take 'em off!

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.380
You have to take
them off, Perrine-san!

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.590
I-I'm totally fi-

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.640
I know I told Perrine
I was good for now,

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:46.260
but sometimes it's nice
to have a full-body soak.

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:48.770
Lucchini-san!

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:50.350
Where's the bug?

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:51.190
Perrine?

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:54.480
Sakamoto-san?

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.820
M-M-Major...

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:58.480
There it is!

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.040
A power outage?

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:31.100
Geez, all this over
a bug? You worried me.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:34.940
But see, the bug went into our pants.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:36.520
It was crawling around...

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:37.690
Exactly!

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:40.780
That vile little insect
embarrassed me!

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:42.360
It's as good as dead!

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:44.450
Hey, that's my bug you're talking about.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:46.700
All right. Let's try and catch it.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:48.240
Wh-What?

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.090
Bah! Bah!

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.340
What a lousy day.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:04.220
I found it! It's heading over there!

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:04.930
Something's going on.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:05.970
It's going that way!

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:07.260
Bug!

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:08.220
I don't want to do this!

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:09.970
Where are you, you repulsive pest?

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:11.310
Are we sure it went this way?

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:13.640
What is all that racket?!

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.390
Barkhorn-san.

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:18.980
Making so much noise in the living
quarters is grounds for disciplinary action.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:20.190
Ah! There it is!

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:21.020
Bug!

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:21.730
Bug?

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:25.820
What about a bug? Just who is responsible for all this-

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:28.370
Oh, it went into the Captain's pants.

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:29.450
Barkhorn-san!

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:30.780
Shut up!

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:35.370
In battle, the ability to make calm decisions
can be the difference between life and death.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.540
In a situation like this, first you must do...

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.170
This!

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:43.210
Got it!

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:47.590
Too slow.

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:49.340
H-Hartmann...

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:51.010
Ah! It's getting away!

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.390
Bug!

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:53.390
Halt!

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:53.850
Damn you!

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:55.390
Bug!

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:00.400
G-Girls...

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:11.780
That's all my work for today.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:17.710
Mio did say it'd be good for
me to take a nice, warm bath.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:21.170
So it's not a normal bug?

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:24.000
I thought it was normal at first, but...

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:27.760
For some reason, wherever it goes, the power goes out.

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:29.300
I won't let it go unpunished!

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.590
Hey, that's my bug
you're talking about.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:31.640
Major!

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:35.140
If this continues unabated,
it could shut down the entire base.

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:36.770
That's true.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.940
But how do we go about locating it?

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.440
It's my bug!

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:41.520
I'm two steps ahead of you!

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:42.060
Huh?

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:43.070
Shirley-san?

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:44.400
Shirley!

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:47.030
I heard you guys talking.

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:49.450
I analyzed the energy
flow inside the base.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:52.120
It's possible that, before
it causes the outages,

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:56.660
the bug emits a special radio frequency and drains electricity from the wires.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:59.410
But then why does it
keep going for our butts?

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.580
I have no idea.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:03.670
I see.

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:08.090
Well, I guess we should
all take our pants off, huh?

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:08.800
No.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:11.510
Do that, and we'll
never catch the bug.

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:13.800
Also, Shirley, what's that
device you're holding?

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:19.810
I built a radio wave detector,
thinking this might be the case.

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:23.610
I even customized the frequency to match the one the bug outputs.

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:26.110
I call it a Bug Detector!

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:31.030
Oh, it's picking it up. It's here.

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:32.070
Huh?

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:34.070
Without a doubt, it's close.

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:42.250
N-Not me!

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.540
There!

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:49.420
No!

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.510
Yoshika-chan!

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:52.630
My bug!

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.470
Wait!

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:58.100
Ew! It's crawling around!

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.560
Miyafuji! Take off your pants!

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:01.310
No!

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:03.150
For everyone's sake, take them off!

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.730
Absolutely not!

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:19.200
Ow-ow-ow...

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:23.670
The detector!

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:24.500
Over there!

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:25.750
The bug's getting away.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:27.000
All right! After it!

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.590
My bug!

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:35.340
Oh, right. I know what we can use.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:39.850
It sure is dark.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:44.230
I wonder if maybe the maintenance
group hasn't finished the lighting yet.

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:55.820
Found 'em. Now we can search for it, even without power.

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:57.570
It's picking it up.

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:00.910
Oh... This way, huh?

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:03.160
Huh?

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:05.500
S-Sanya?

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.040
No wait, it's way, way past Sanya...

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:10.300
Right?

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:15.300
<i>It can't be. It couldn't be...</i>

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:16.550
<i>Right?</i>

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:21.560
<i>But it is possible it's there, so...</i>

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:29.060
<i>Here goes.</i>

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:41.280
Th-That's something else!

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:44.290
Eila...

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:03.100
A-Anyway, Sanya thinks she's
sensing the Neuroi's presence.

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:05.140
I'm not 100% certain yet,

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:06.890
but I'm sensing it in the
airspace above the base,

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.600
as well as inside this building.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.150
Inside this building?

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.940
Could the bug be a Neuroi?

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:13.280
Huh?

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:18.030
Eila, Sanya, help out by
searching the building.

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:18.910
Roger.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:22.580
Barkhorn and Hartmann, prepare to
intercept the Neuroi above the base.

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:23.490
Roger.

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:25.660
Miyafuji, come with me!

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:26.660
Yes, ma'am!

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:41.510
Neuroi spotted.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:43.010
Sakamoto-san!

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:44.890
Captain Minna isn't in her room!

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:45.930
What?

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:47.640
We have no choice. I'm
sounding the emergency alarm.

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:55.610
Damn, did they knock out the entire electrical system?

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:59.240
Miyafuji, go to the hangar and
inform Barkhorn and Hartmann.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:18:59.820
Yes, ma'am!

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:13.790
Over there.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:14.630
That way, huh?

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:22.890
If I were a bug, I'd probably come to a place like this.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:25.220
Once I find it, that bug is so dead!

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:28.220
Huh? Did it get you again, Perrine-san?

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:30.230
I-It's nothing.

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:31.690
Found it.

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:32.230
Huh?

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:33.810
It's inside you, Perrine.

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:37.400
N-N-No, it isn't! It isn't!

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:38.360
Perrine-san...

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.280
I said it isn't!

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:41.360
Then take your pants off.

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:45.580
A-All right...

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:47.450
Target acquired.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.450
Roger that. I'm on standby.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:52.000
Now!

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.540
Fire!

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:01.130
Score!

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:02.090
Did we get her?

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:03.800
Ah! The bug!

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:06.350
My bug!

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:07.930
We have to catch it.

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.060
It went over there.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:11.020
My bug!

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:12.480
Hold it right there!

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:14.690
H-Hey! Halt, you-

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:15.730
Perrine-san?

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:18.730
This is an emergency
announcement from Major Sakamoto.

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:21.860
She can't detect a core
in the mid-air Neuroi's,

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:23.780
but we cannot wait any longer.

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:26.830
She'd like you two to intercept it at once.

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:27.740
Roger!

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:32.620
Also, a flying object has taken
out the base's electrical system.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:34.750
She asks you to be extra careful, given this.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:38.250
She must mean that weird bug that was flying into everyone's pants.

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:40.630
We were just discussing the
perfect countermeasure for it.

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:46.970
Let's go, Hartmann!

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:48.640
It's so breezy!

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:54.390
That way!

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:57.480
S-Sakamoto-san!

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:00.280
Barkhorn-san and
Hartmann-san left to engage it.

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:00.860
Excellent.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:04.280
This way!

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:22.670
Just like Mio said,

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:24.220
that really melted away my exhaustion.

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:28.010
That's it.

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:28.720
Right there.

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:29.260
There!

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:31.510
H-Hey!

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:32.970
Now's my chance!

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:36.350
I see it!

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:51.200
Huh?

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:52.450
Well done, Minna.

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:53.580
You did it!

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.500
I-Incredible work.

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:58.460
Ah! My bug!

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:01.460
Wh-What on earth is going on?
My poor little bug was crushed...

00:22:07.550 --> 00:22:08.930
The Neuroi...

00:22:08.930 --> 00:22:10.890
It vanished without us even doing anything?

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:15.730
This is Sakamoto.
We destroyed the core down here.

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:17.690
The mid-air Neuroi wasn't the main body.

00:22:17.690 --> 00:22:19.060
Return to base at once.

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:20.360
Huh?

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:22.820
Roger that. Mission complete.

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:24.820
Ah-choo!

00:22:28.360 --> 00:22:29.700
A few days later,

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:34.290
Lieutenant Colonel Minna Dietlinde Wilcke was awarded this medal

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:36.120
for shooting down her 200th Neuroi.

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:15.350
No way... What happened to me?

00:24:15.350 --> 00:24:17.640
I can't protect anyone like this!

00:24:17.930 --> 00:24:20.270
Wait! Everyone, please wait!

00:24:20.270 --> 00:24:24.650
Next time on <i>Strike Witches 2:</i> Please Grant Me Wings.
